{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The Trends summary. A range is 7, 30 or 90 calendar days ending with today, and today counts. Only days with at least one entry count: a day with nothing logged is left out and never read as 0. A logged day with no known value for a measure has no value for it and is left out of that measure. kcal uses the goal in force today for every day, because the chart draws one goal line. A band is under below 90% of the target, over above 110%, otherwise on_target (the edges are on target). 7D and 30D have one bar per day. 90D has 7-day bars counted back from today, so the oldest bar covers the 6 days left over, and a bar's value is the mean of its days with a value. bars lists only bars with a value; bar_count counts all of them. top is the larger of 125% of the kcal target, the known bars and the known weekdays, and at least 1. Weekdays run Monday to Sunday and hold the mean of the days with a value; over means above 105% of the target. Ties for highest and lowest take the earlier date. difference is average minus target. Values are unrounded.",
